{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Your seal, your cord, and your staff that is in your hand.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): 'your seal' — the ring with which you seal. Perhaps upon Judah's seal was the figure of a lion, on account of 'גור אריה יהודה' — 'a lion's whelp is Judah.' 'Your cord' — Rashi explained it as your garment with which you cover yourself. And Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote concerning this that it is not correct, for it would mean that Judah gives his garment and goes naked from her; and how could Scripture call a garment 'cord' and say concerning it 'the seal, and the cords'? And if you would say it is named after the cords of tsitsit, Heaven forbid that Judah would treat the commandment of tsitsit lightly to give it as a harlot's fee. Therefore he, of blessed memory, explained 'your cord' as a small scarf with which one wraps part of the head, and even today it is the custom of nobles in the eastern lands to spread it over their heads; and it is called 'cord' because it is short like a cord; and it is translated שושיפא, as in the Targum (Deuteronomy 22:17), 'and spread the garment — שושיפא.'" "<b>And your staff.</b> The staff that is in his hand, after the custom of princes, in the manner of what is written (Ezekiel 19:14): 'מטה עוז שבט למשול' — 'a strong rod, a scepter for ruling.' And it is written (Genesis 49:10): 'לא יסור שבט מיהודה' — 'the scepter shall not depart from Judah.'" "<b>And there are</b> those who explained that in these three things which she asked of him as a pledge, she alluded to him the matter of food (she'er), clothing (kesut), and conjugal rights ('onah). 'Your seal' — this is conjugal rights (onah), for the organ is sealed with the sign of the holy covenant. 'Your cord' — this is clothing (kesut). 'And your staff' — this is food (she'er), which is sustenance, as it is written (Leviticus 26:26): 'בשברי לכם מטה לחם' — 'when I break for you the staff of bread.'" "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> 'Your seal, your cord, and your staff' — all three were fulfilled in her. 'Your seal' — that there came forth from her Zerubbabel, of whom it is written (Haggai 2:23): 'ושמתיך כחותם כי בך בחרתי נאם ה׳ צבאות' — 'and I will set you as a seal, for you I have chosen, says YHWH of Hosts.' 'Your cord' — that there came forth from her Bezalel, of whom it is written (Exodus 39:3): 'וקצץ פתילים' — 'and they cut threads.' 'And your staff' — that there came forth from her David, of whom it is written (I Samuel): 'ויקח מקלו בידו' — 'and he took his staff in his hand.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:46.520846276Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}